WEBVTT

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.750
Let's just leave aside what happened last week.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:10.300
Since we were told of suspicious events on the Moon,

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.370
we're on patrol there.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:16.700
But such uneventful routine work...

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.660
There are good things and bad things about this.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.790
The first star! I found it!

00:01:58.790 --> 00:01:59.840
Now listen, Ryoko.

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:01.640
It doesn't matter how,

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.800
but I want you to find the first star that shines insides yourself.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:04.310
What's that?

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.660
Something that you can say you're the best at.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.230
Something at which you can shine brighter than anyone else.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:11.590
A person with that inside will have a life filled with happiness.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:21.150
The first star inside myself...

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:26.860
Hello!

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:31.220
Stupid dream.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:37.000
You're the Next "Captain" of the Nadesico!

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:37.970
Darn.

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:43.970
First Star! First Star!

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:47.120
First Stars everywhere!

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.820
First... Star...

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:52.600
A First Star is excellent.

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:56.620
Oh yeah, it rules.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.740
Delivery service!  Thanks for waiting!

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:01.410
What do you say? Why don't you give this contest a shot?

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.320
What is all of this?

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:05.510
This!

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:07.220
Posters.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.130
That's not what I mean!

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.170
A girl.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:16.380
The girl who becomes the First Star gets to debut as an idol!

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:18.450
Hear that? An idol!

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:19.040
Really?

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.470
Where did this come from?

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:23.970
Without my permission, out of the blue?!

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.760
It's for the sake of everyone's future.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.800
While they are currently entangled in war,

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:33.110
the crew of Nadesico are everyday young people.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:35.310
I felt they should start preparations toward a career

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:39.450
they could hope for after the war with Jupiter ends.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:40.840
This is one of those plans.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:42.280
Jobs for after the war?

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:46.720
Yes! We are not fighting for the sake of fighting.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:51.410
Instead, peace, hope, and the first star of happiness are the things which we are fighting to win!

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:52.860
I see.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.540
"Happiness won't come walking toward you.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.510
That's why you need to walk toward it."

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:58.250
There is that old saying. I see.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:00.800
Well in that case, I'm all for it!

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:01.410
Yes!

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:01.700
Yes, yes! Just wonderful! Maybe I should even try myself?

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:04.550
Why don't we let the First Star be the captain as well?

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:09.140
No, never mind. You are the captain, after all.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:09.940
I see!

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:14.260
Idol stars become mayor or police chief for a day all the time.

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:16.020
A "Captain for a Day" sounds just fine.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.350
Yes, it makes it all the more like an idol contest!

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:24.300
So, all those girls that want to become idol stars after the war with Jupiter, don't hesitate to apply!

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:27.770
The first star will become captain of the Nadesico for a day!

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:29.450
This has been an urgent message from the Captain!

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:31.280
A new captain!

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:33.520
A captain, a kanchou!

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:36.020
A kanchou? You mean a spy?

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:38.270
Kan  Chou

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:39.540
What? Has she cracked another pun?

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:41.210
Hardly anyone uses that expression any more.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.510
Does anyone even remember that "kanchou"

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:44.630
is an old-fashioned way to describe a spy in Japanese?

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:47.060
But now you've learned something new!

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:47.890
Who are you talking to?

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:48.550
Bye!

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:55.210
So, so, Ryoko, what will you do as a stunt?

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:56.140
A song? Some trick?

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:57.600
I'm not doing either.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.270
Why, why? You get to be an idol star.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.160
Come on, let's do it.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:04.430
It's a chance for you to become an idol!

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:05.970
Not interested in the least.

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:07.010
Oh, okay...

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:07.520
Jeez, we won't be able to go as the Gekiganger team without you.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:12.010
What are you going to do after the fighting is over?

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:13.110
What are you going to do?

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.620
Houmei-san, would you inspect my soup?

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:16.380
Ever thought about it?

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:18.850
Not bad.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.690
Wha, what the hell is this?!

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:24.010
Wondering about someone?!

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:26.470
Someone not Houmei-san?

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:27.260
You jerks!

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:42.940
Houmei and the Houmei Girls!

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:46.020
So, time to get to work and keep busy, oh boy!

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:47.920
Hey, let me in too!

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:49.070
What's all the noise?

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:49.490
Are the kids here getting excited too?

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:51.120
Oh no, it's spilling out!

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:53.880
But there are no more dishes to wash.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:54.850
Guess it's all done.

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:55.500
What about outfits?

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:56.630
even for a short while.

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:03.620
Yes, you've passed the first selection process.

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:05.250
Oh, so close, but not this time.

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:06.380
Next one...

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:08.110
SO! How is it coming along, Prospector-kun?

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:11.750
Make sure that our new captain just oozes teen idol-ness.

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:13.120
I fully understand! Really!

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:14.540
Since the recent confidential information leak,

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.670
the number of crewmembers leaving the ship has increased greatly.

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:21.360
As a company, we would love to boost the ship's image at low cost.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.590
I came up with this project, so I'm counting on you.

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:27.940
From toddlers to senior citizens and beyond,
we need a super idol that captures all their hearts!

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:31.470
A happy Nadesico with a new captain! Happy, happy, right?!

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:32.700
Even the top brass in the military have...

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:39.060
Why is that ad agencies are so preoccupied with their clients?

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.120
Excuse me.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:43.460
It seems that some misinformation is going around.

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:46.320
This isn't a contest for a new captain, is it?

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.630
I must take care of all the applicants here.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:51.850
Wouldn't it be a good idea to make a clarification immediately?

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:53.050
Clarification?

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:57.580
Everyone is starting to think they'll be the new captain,
instead of being captain for a day.

00:06:57.580 --> 00:06:59.040
There's no cause for alarm on that account.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:04.230
Your appearance! Your kindness! Your glowing smile!

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.440
Without question, you'll be the one chosen in the end.

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:07.900
Misumaru Yurika!

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:14.660
Ladies and Gentlemen!

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:18.660
And now Nadesico's "First Star: You are the Next Captain of Tomorrow!"

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:22.290
Our lineup starts up a pilot with cute glasses, Amano Hikaru-san!

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.910
Hikaru sings for us "V is for Victory, Gekiganger V,"

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:27.810
the opening theme to "Hot Blooded Robot: Gekiganger V!"

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:36.540
The "New captain contest" is finally starting.

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:39.850
This contest is broadcasting around Nadesico.

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:42.640
We'll also follow the contestant's popularity polls.

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:46.240
With me is former heavyweight champion playboy, Akatsuki Nagare-san.

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:47.270
Hello.

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:49.630
Who is the playboy?

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:51.990
Megu-chan?

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:54.850
What will you do with that uniform?

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:57.400
Actually, I trained as a nurse before becoming a voice actress,

00:07:57.400 --> 00:07:59.440
so I thought I'd do a nutritional IV injection.

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:01.700
IV means intravenous, right?

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:02.580
That's right.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:04.150
Are you certified?

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:06.630
Okay, let's have your arm now.

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:08.590
Oh, no, a needle is not something you lick, dear.

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:11.740
Idle talk, idle talk,

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:15.040
Idle be next on stage.

00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:24.170
Next, Minato-san with her swimsuit competition trial!

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:33.990
White monk!

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:38.550
First star, I found it.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:40.210
It goes boing, boing, boing...

00:08:40.210 --> 00:08:42.720
It looks pretty hopeless for lzumi-chan.

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:44.370
Who's in the lead, Akatsuki-san?

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:45.570
Let me see...

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:46.990
Let's go to our next contestant.

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:49.130
I'm going to inject you.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.790
But there's no needle, because it's too dangerous, okay?

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:55.470
Wow, votes for Megu-chan are coming in fast! Who's next?

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:58.390
Oh, aren't those the Houmei Girls?

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:01.210
It looks like they might be strong contenders, Uribatake-san.

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:03.500
They might just pull off an upset, Akatsuki-san.

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:08.500
I like this.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:10.400
Everyone's shining so bright.

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:11.820
They're not at all like the cold Jovians,

00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:14.440
who only think about fighting all the time.

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:23.740
Thanks for waiting! We now present our star of stars,

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:27.770
entry number 1578, Misumaru Yurika-san!

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:28.180
We don't even have 1500 people!
entry number 1578, Misumaru Yurika-san!

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:28.710
We don't even have 1500 people!

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:30.620
The lily blossoming in space.

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:32.200
Shining with lovely radiance,

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:34.030
here's everyone's charming first star.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:36.050
Let's have her sing for us!

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:40.970
Banner by: Aoi Jun
Being Myself

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:35.440
L! O! V! E! Lovely Yurika!

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:58.460
Auto Pirot : ON

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:13.410
You're warm as well.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:16.370
Being myself? For me?

00:11:21.230 --> 00:11:21.800
Bridge!

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:33.670
Thank you, thank you.

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:35.200
Come on now!

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:49.270
I know this is sudden, but I'd like to sing.

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:59.170
Banner by: Omoikane
I Want to Be Your Number One

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:55.460
Ruri-chan!

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:58.530
She's going to stand out.

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:32.560
Was it my imagination?

00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:39.150
Something is not right.

00:13:39.970 --> 00:13:42.830
Something that can't be picked up by Nadesico's sensors.

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:04.530
Stage Effects: Omoikane

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:07.110
Wow! I never thought Ruri could pull off something like this.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:08.210
What is it with the smoke?

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:09.450
I think Omoikane is playing favorites here.

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:46.990
You did it, Ruri-chan!

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:48.470
I never would have imagined.

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:50.450
Thank you, sorry for interrupting.

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:54.900
Well, now this upsets everything! Right, Uribatake-san?!

00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:56.080
You're frothing at the mike.

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:00.330
You did a great job, Ruri-chan!

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:09.380
Guess it was nothing.

00:15:10.270 --> 00:15:11.970
They're not at all like the cold Jovians,

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:14.560
who only think about fighting all the time.

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:19.550
So, what am I supposed to do?

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:21.890
A missile?

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:24.790
Human?!

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:30.450
What the hell is this?

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:33.260
Damn!

00:15:35.610 --> 00:15:36.830
Emergency

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:39.540
An explosion in space ahead of the ship.

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:41.710
Ryoko-san's Aestivalis is already deployed.

00:15:42.070 --> 00:15:44.000
Damn, how could we have completely missed it?

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:45.420
Ryoko...

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:49.960
What the hell is with these guys?!

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:56.220
Missiles with human onboard?

00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:59.020
It looks like the enemy has been conducting

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:00.760
experiments with long distance boson jumping.

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:04.440
They can warp in without support, then explode.

00:16:06.220 --> 00:16:08.560
If this system works out, it will become a great threat to us.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.760
Wow, we've just had her go through her patent explanation routine

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:14.470
while dressed elegantly in her swimwear attire.

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:15.920
The glamour of a mature lady?

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:17.330
So that's how you do it, Inez-san!

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:19.420
Hey, wait a minute. I have to get going!

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:20.310
I'm supposed to be out there!

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:39.170
Incoming!

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:40.930
Ryoko-chan, why did you take off alone without telling anyone?

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:41.430
Get out of my way!

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:50.690
Fighting's the only thing I can do right!

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:55.340
Another one.

00:16:55.650 --> 00:16:58.040
What's wrong with that?! That's just your first star!

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:00.010
You're shining right now. What's wrong with that?

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:00.820
Everything, of course!

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:05.070
They were humans too.

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:09.500
In the end, all I do is kill people.

00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:12.730
Three remaining units have arrived in the combat area.

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:14.090
Ryoko-chan...

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:17.100
But take that away from me and I have nothing left.

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:20.230
After all I've been through, to find out this is my first star?

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:22.360
If that's all I have,

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:23.930
then nothing will be lost when I'm gone!

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:24.850
Don't say that!

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:26.730
If you were gone...

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:29.020
If Ryoko-chan was ever taken away from me, I'd be sad!

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:30.150
I'm sure everyone else would be sad as well!

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:31.190
Same goes for me!

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:32.000
Me too!

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:33.440
Same here.

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:34.740
That's why you can't say that!

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:35.700
What's wrong with being good at this?

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:39.780
Humanoid fighter craft ahead. They've increased to four.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:41.540
Should we alter our mission?

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:43.620
No, we will continue on.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:46.210
All of you must make it back with the data.

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:48.260
This is only a test run.

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:49.620
Don't push it, boys.

00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:50.570
Roger!

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:54.900
If you asked me why I fight, I could only say

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:57.060
that it's because I don't know of a good alternative to follow.

00:17:57.370 --> 00:17:59.050
But I do not think that justifies this.

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:02.800
These chairs were much too small, right, Akatsuki-san?

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:04.150
Seems like we're stuck.

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:08.330
Fighting is the only thing I can do right now as well!

00:18:08.680 --> 00:18:09.480
For now, at least.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:12.400
I'm sure you'll find something else, someday.

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:17.340
All units spread out!

00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:27.260
Operations, request retrieval, Sir.

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:28.730
Okay, just hold tight.

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:31.310
Don't you dare come back!

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:35.320
I'll find it. Maybe I can't stop to do that now, but...

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:40.060
Are you all right, Ryoko-chan?

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:41.490
Knock it off, Idiot.

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:42.840
I can manage on my own just fine!

00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:44.510
No, you can't. You've been beaten up pretty badly.

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:46.130
You think so?

00:18:46.130 --> 00:18:47.960
Looks like it. Let me help you.

00:18:49.030 --> 00:18:49.880
Hey, thanks.

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:50.880
It's too bad.

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:54.080
You should have participated in the Nadesico idol contest as well.

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:55.690
The expression on your face right now is golden.

00:18:56.040 --> 00:18:58.530
You're... You're out of your mind!

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:01.190
What did you do that for?!

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:05.100
There goes Akito-san again.

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:10.960
Maybe I was able to find my first star.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:14.070
Tenkawa, beyond the range of the energy feed,

00:19:14.070 --> 00:19:15.330
and becomes the first star.

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:17.370
What was that?!

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:20.140
Fellow crewmembers of the Nadesico, the wait is over.

00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:22.090
We will now announce the results!

00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:26.010
Okay! Forgive us, as only the top contestants are listed.

00:19:26.230 --> 00:19:28.180
Wow! Hoshino Ruri-chan is racing up the charts, just as predicted!

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:30.390
Just look at those vote totals climb!

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:30.790
Please Wait for a While

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:33.520
How much longer until the results come back from the Nadesico?

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:35.940
Yes, well, it should be any minute now.

00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:40.240
I just hope that the next captain will be a young, cute,

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:42.860
and ditzy idol that will get the crew's attention off of the leak.

00:19:43.250 --> 00:19:44.440
Setting aside the question of being a ditz,

00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:46.740
that Misumaru Yurika is just too homely, and looks as if

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:49.270
she might affiliate herself with the pacifist movement.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:53.210
Why don't we figure out a new slogan while we wait?

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:56.740
How about a poster where the captain has her index fingers together like this, reading,

00:19:56.740 --> 00:19:59.480
"Naughty kids that won't fight will get it from Captain Enema!"

00:19:59.480 --> 00:20:00.490
Ikeda, out, now!

00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:00.950
What?

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:01.280
Please Wait for a While

00:20:01.280 --> 00:20:03.110
How about, "Love, Love Battle Girl"?

00:20:03.110 --> 00:20:04.550
"Nadesico: Do You Remonstrate Love"?

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:06.110
"I love you, so protect me."

00:20:06.110 --> 00:20:07.270
How about "Oh my", or "Hey".

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:07.680
Please Wait for a While

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:08.970
Isn't Ruri-chan just wonderful?

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:11.420
Loading Data

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:12.890
"You're the New Captain!" Contest Result

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:15.900
Isn't Ruri-chan so dreamy?

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:22.500
With the winner Hoshino Ruri abstaining for personal reasons,

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:25.750
the award went to the winner of a "rock, paper, scissors" match.

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:29.110
Emerging as the winner,
Misumaru Yurika will continue as captain.

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:30.020
That's all.

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:30.740
What?!

00:20:31.610 --> 00:20:38.880
Please let me be your very own, your number one...

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:41.140
Or so they say.

00:21:44.140 --> 00:21:46.710
Let me do some explaining in the time we have left.

00:21:46.710 --> 00:21:48.810
The runaway hit anime show on board the Nadesico, Gekiganger 3,

00:21:48.810 --> 00:21:51.060
is a TV anime made about one hundred years ago.

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:54.290
The people who were banished to Jupiter had copies of this show,

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:56.860
allowing them to become infatuated with it.

00:21:56.860 --> 00:21:58.700
But since the preservation of the tapes was incomplete,

00:21:58.700 --> 00:22:01.790
some episodes have been lost, only to be known in legend.

00:22:01.790 --> 00:22:05.460
Oops, I'll explain the rest about this next time.

00:22:05.460 --> 00:22:07.340
The next episode of Martian Successor Nadesico is:

00:22:07.620 --> 00:22:09.300
"Run Silent, Run Deep"

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:10.970
Everyone listen in for more explanations!
